      "problem": "Write the equation of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}=24$ in standard form.",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $24$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2} & =24 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{24}-\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{24} & =\\frac{24}{24} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
